 "transcript": [
  "[action] The second son sets up his grain market.",
  "[silence] the second son says nothing.",
  "[says] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung asks about the eldest son's new wife.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Now what kind of woman is this new one of yours?\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"She is a woman with silver and gold and a woman of good birth,\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and I am glad of it. We may be rich and the great men of the town may court me with their daughters, but we are still men of the fields and the blood of our fathers is in us. I would not have my sons marry women who are not worthy of them,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"So be it, my son. I would not have you marry any woman who was not fit for you.\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and I would like to see her and to hear of her,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"She is a woman with a good heart and a kind one,\"",
  "Wang Lung: \"Well, and it is a good thing she is a kind one, since you do not know her heart.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung sleeps, exhausted.",
